{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-substrate-parameter-unique","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Theorem","doco:Section"],"label":"thm:substrate-parameter-unique","kind":"theorem","title":"Uniqueness of the substrate parameter","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-substrate-parameter-exists","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-braiding-eigenvalue-extraction","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-positive-definite-dagger"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-substrate-parameter-unique"],"tags":["uniqueness","substrate","deformation"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.SubstrateParameter.unique","text":"substrate-parameter-unique.md","leanSource":"substrate-parameter-unique.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"thm:substrate-parameter-unique\"></a><p>Given a QOU <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code>, the substrate parameter <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\in \\mathrm{End}(\\mathbf{1})</code> is uniquely determined <em>as a parameter</em>: the braiding spectrum and the positive-definite dagger select exactly one scalar from the Hecke eigenvalue pair <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\{q, -q^{-1}\\}</code> (the positive one).  This is parameter uniqueness — the <em>extraction procedure</em> is canonical, with no ambiguity or choice.  It does <em>not</em> mean <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> takes a single value.  The substrate parameter is a field <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\colon M \\to \\mathbb{R}_{>0}</code> that varies across the manifold and with energy scale; high-energy processes see a different <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> than low-energy ones.  The observed value <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q_0</code> at the location and energy of observation is empirical.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-unique.md","heading":"Theorem","number":"4.7.9","page":"b/thm-substrate-parameter-unique","qa":{"counts":{"pass":90,"fail":2,"warn":1,"na":11,"unknown":0,"stale":103},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":1}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.SubstrateParameter.unique","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-unique.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
